Jeff,
This is all the best information I have for Serious Shea Burkina Faso and
CLEO.  In the meantime I am filling a PDI manually for Senegal as it's
complicated.
I think we do the Serious Shea Burkina Faso only for Shea supply chain with
the detailed Serious Shea model with respect to Business and Usual for
Burkina Faso only, % exported as kernels and % exported as sheabutter
cosmetic grade/food and confectionary grade.  Then later we can look at
'Shea International' for the other West African Countries.

Attached is the most up to date Business Plan and Financial Plan 2021. This
has a non-disclosure agreement so we cannot attach to the documents just
extract the information. It was the investment that the DFC (US Development
Finance) would not give us in the end because of the Coup d'Etat in
Burkina. It has some excellent info. attached including a market survey for
prices paid by cosmetic brands further up the supply chain, so all data
needs to be extracted.

In summary attached says, if we secured US$10m in financing from DFC, we
could construct 8 x collection sites and 4 x processing centres in 2021/22.
We would produce 2,400t of unrefined shea butter for export in 2022,
employing 1,280 staff (mostly women) and changing the lives of over 10,000
women processors (offering 1.5x higher prices, 10% profit share, and
healthy working conditions). We would also save over 60,000tCO2e of GHG
emissions each year through reduce deforestation and zero wood burn. And
the business would be profitable and self-sustaining!

These documents below in the email window are all the due diligence funded
by the African Development Bank, the World Bank and the Burkina Faso
Government. All the information needs extracting and perhaps also tied to
steps to achieve the Sustainable Development Goal Indicators, a list of
which are here
https://claritycoalition.net/knowledge-base/sustainable-development-goals-2=
026/

There is some excellent granular data, maps in the zip below. Including a
survey of all the women's groups and the lead person for each group.


