Average amount processed by 1 women per month: 12 bags shea (whole fruits
or kernels?) per MT;  7 bags processed per woman per month =3D 0.53 MT; 7
bags produce 187 kg shea butter; conversion rate is 0.53/0.187 =3D 2.834

The Shea season lasts 5 months from May to October, meaning one woman would
produce in the region of 5*187kg =3D 925kg

At the end of 2013, the price of shea nuts was 250 CFA francs per kilogram
(Rousseau et al., 2015).  Therefore price per MT with x-rate at 0.0017
CFA:1 US$ 250000*0.0017=3D MT  425 US$ nuts.


